    "questionEn": "A photoemissive substance is illuminated with a radiation of wavelength λ i so that it releases electrons with de-Broglie wavelength λ e . The longest wavelength of radiation that can emit photoelectron is λ o . Expression for de-Broglie wavelength is given by: (m: mass of the electron, h: Planck's constant and c: speed of light)",
