    "explanationEn": "Given Information: Force: F ⃗ = ( 2 t i ˆ + 3 t 2 j ˆ ) N Mass of the object, m = 1000 g = 1 kg Determine Acceleration: Using Newton's second law, F → = m a → . Thus, the acceleration, a → = 2 t i ˆ + 3 t 2 j ˆ . Velocity Calculation: To find velocity, integrate acceleration with respect to time: d v → d t = 2 t i ˆ + 3 t 2 j ˆ Integrate to find v → : v → = ∫ ( 2 t i ˆ + 3 t 2 j ˆ ) d t = t 2 i ˆ + t 3 j ˆ + C ⃗ (Assuming initial velocity is zero, C ⃗ = 0 , hence v → = t 2 i ˆ + t 3 j ˆ ). Calculate Power: Power is defined as the dot product of force and velocity vectors: P = F → ⋅ v → = ( 2 t i ˆ + 3 t 2 j ˆ ) ⋅ ( t 2 i ˆ + t 3 j ˆ ) Computing the dot product gives: P = ( 2 t ⋅ t 2 ) + ( 3 t 2 ⋅ t 3 ) = 2 t 3 + 3 t 5 The power generated at time t is P = ( 2 t 3 + 3 t 5 ) W .",
