    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "Determine one main scale division (msd): 300 msd = 15 cm Therefore, 1 msd = 15 300 cm = 0.05 cm Determine one vernier scale division (vsd): 25 vsd = 24 msd Therefore, 1 vsd = 24 25 msd Calculate the least count (LC): The least count is given by the difference between one main scale division and one vernier scale division: LC = 1 msd − 1 vsd Substitute the expression for 1 vsd: LC = 1 msd − 24 25 × 1 msd This simplifies to: LC = 1 25 × 1 msd Calculate the LC in cm: Substituting the value of 1 msd: LC = 1 25 × 0.05 cm = 0.002 cm Hence, the least count of the traveling microscope is 0.002 cm.",
