    "questionEn": "In a reaction A + B → C , initial concentrations of A and B are related as [ A ] 0 = 8 [ B ] 0 . The half lives of A and B are 10 min and 40 min , respectively. If they start to disappear at the same time, both following first order kinetics, after how much time will the concentration of both the reactants be same?",
