    "date": "Wed, 2 Apr 2025",
    "shift": 1,
    "subject": "Chemistry",
    "questionEn": "Consider the following electrochemical cell at standard condition. Au ( s ) | QH 2 , Q | NH 4 X ( 0.01 M ) | | Ag + ( 1 M ) ∣ Ag ( s ) E cell = + 0.4 V The couple QH 2 / Q represents quinhydrone electrode, the half cell reaction is given below: [ Given : E 0 Ag + / Ag = + 0.8 V and 2.303 RT F = 0.06 V ] The pK b value of the ammonium halide salt ( NH 4 X ) used here is __________ . (nearest integer)",
